# Bundle G — Public / community. NOT ACTIVE.
#
# This is an example. Enable it only on a public repository:
#
#   git mv .github/bundles/community/llms.txt.example llms.txt
#
# llms.txt is a convention, not a standard and not a control. It is a hint at
# the repository root telling a crawler or an assistant which documents matter
# and in what order. Nothing enforces it, nothing checks it, and no model is
# obliged to read it.
#
# Which is why this is a public-only file. On a private repository it protects
# nothing (access control already did that) and it documents your layout to
# whoever eventually gets the clone. It is also NOT a place to write
# instructions for assistants working *in* the repository — that is AGENTS.md,
# and it is already active.
#
# Replace REPO_NAME, the summary, and the URLs before enabling. Delete every
# line of this comment block: the file is meant to be read, and a reader who
# hits fifteen lines of caveats stops at line two.

# REPO_NAME

> One sentence saying what this repository is and who it is for. Written for
> someone who arrived from a search result and has thirty seconds.

This repository documents itself in its wiki. The pages below are the source of
truth; anything else in the tree is implementation.

## Docs

- [README](https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/blob/main/README.md): what this is, and how to use it
- [Getting Started](https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/wiki/Getting-Started): setup, end to end
- [Architecture Decisions](https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/wiki/Architecture-Decisions): why it is shaped this way
- [Contributing](https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md): branch, commit, and pull request conventions

## Optional

- [Changelog](https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md): what changed and when
- [Security policy](https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/blob/main/SECURITY.md): reporting a vulnerability
- [Support](https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/blob/main/SUPPORT.md): where to ask a question
